              <a href={emailHref} class="cta-btn cta-btn-mail">Send email</a>
            </div>

            <h2 id="technician-visit">What to Expect During a Visit from a RotoRem Technician</h2>
            <p>At RotoRem, we believe in providing a transparent and convenient service. The repair process is organised to make everything as easy as possible for you:</p>
            <ol>
              <li><strong>Service request and consultation:</strong> Contact us and describe the problem. For example: "The oven is locked and the key symbol is illuminated" or "The fan is working, but the oven is not heating up."</li>
              <li><strong>Visit at a convenient time:</strong> A technician comes directly to your address, saving you the trouble of transporting a heavy appliance to a repair centre.</li>
              <li><strong>Diagnosis and quotation:</strong> The technician inspects the oven's components, explains the cause of the fault and provides the total price for the repair and any required parts.</li>
              <li><strong>Repair with a warranty:</strong> In most cases, the fault can be repaired during the first visit. Once the work has been completed, the appliance is tested in front of you. A warranty is provided according to the type of repair carried out.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2 id="prevention">How to Prevent the Problem from Recurring</h2>
            <p>Follow these simple operating guidelines to help your Gorenje oven work reliably for many years:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Avoid using aggressive cleaning products on the seals:</strong> Strong chemicals can damage the rubber, causing the oven to lose its airtight seal. This may lead to overheating of the surrounding kitchen units and the touchscreen control panel.</li>
              <li><strong>Ensure proper ventilation:</strong> When installing a new built-in oven, make sure all of the manufacturer's installation and ventilation requirements are followed. Overheating is one of the main causes of damage to electronic circuit boards.</li>
              <li><strong>Do not slam the oven door:</strong> Strong impacts can damage both the glass and the delicate microswitch mechanism connected to the locking system.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              When you are dealing with a persistent problem that you cannot safely resolve yourself, seek professional assistance. You can easily request a visit for professional oven repair in <a href="https://www.rotorem.bg/en/services/sofia/oven-repair/" class="inline-link">Sofia</a> or <a href="https://www.rotorem.bg/en/services/oven-repair/" class="inline-link">Varna</a>.
            </p>

            <div class="cta-inline" role="group" aria-label="Contact options">
              <a href={callHref} class="cta-btn cta-btn-call">Call: 089 834 0982</a>
              <a href={emailHref} class="cta-btn cta-btn-mail">Send email</a>
            </div>

            <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>What Does the F4 Error Code Mean, and Where Can I Find Gorenje's Official Error Code List?</h3>
            <p>
              The F4 error code on a Gorenje oven indicates a fault with the temperature sensor, also known as the PT1000 sensor. The oven's electronic control system has detected either a short circuit in the sensor or a broken connection, meaning that the control board can no longer communicate with it. The most reliable way to identify the meaning of an error message is to consult the official user manual for your specific model. You can find and download the relevant manual from <a href="https://www.gorenje.com/bg/support/user-instructions" class="inline-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gorenje's user instructions page</a>. When the code indicates a serious fault, contact a qualified repair service for a professional diagnosis.
            </p>
            <h3>Is It Normal for the Fan to Continue Running After the Oven Has Been Switched Off?</h3>
            <p>
              Yes. In many ovens, the cooling fan continues to operate for a certain period after the appliance has been switched off. This helps cool the oven casing and electronic components. When the fan continues running for an unusually long time or makes an abnormal noise, a technical inspection is recommended.
            </p>
            <h3>When Should the Oven Door Seal Be Replaced?</h3>
            <p>
              The seal should be replaced when it is cracked, torn, deformed or no longer fits tightly around the door. Excessive heat escaping from around the oven door may also indicate that the seal is worn.
            </p>
            <h3>Is It Worth Repairing a Burnt-Out Oven Heating Element?</h3>
            <p>
              Yes. Replacing a heating element is a standard, relatively quick and cost-effective repair. It can extend the appliance's service life by several years and usually costs considerably less than purchasing a new oven.
            </p>

            <p class="disclaimer">
              This article has been prepared for informational purposes and does not replace professional technical diagnostics.
            </p>
          </div>
